ets and we prove a strong automorphism conjecture for series-parallel ordered sets. We conclude with an example that shows that the automorphism to endomorphism ratio can exceed $\\displaystyle{ \\left( .5244 \\right) ^{|P|}} $ for arbitrarily large $|P|$.\n\nDoes almost every isotone, self-map have a fixed point?\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jan 1991\n\n  * I. Rival\n  * A. Rutkowski\n\nView\n\nIsotone Maps: Enumeration and Structure\n\nArticle\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nThe number of order-preserving maps of fences and crowns\n\nArticle\n\n  * Jan 1991\n\n  * J. D. Currie\n  * T. I. Visentin\n\nWe perform an exact enumeration of the order-preserving maps of fences (zig-zags) and crowns (cycles). From this we derive asymptotic results.\n\nView\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe number of order-preserving maps of fences and crowns - MaRDI portal (https://portal.mardi4nfdi.de/wiki/The_number_of_order-preserving_maps_of_fences_and_crowns)\nciteturn9404search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 34.2 years ago; Crawled: last week; Currie, Terry I.VisentinPublication date 27 June 1992 ... asymptotic posets order-preserving map lattices paths ...   * The rank of the inverse semigroup of all partial automorphisms on a finite crown\n# The number of order-preserving maps of fences and crowns\n\nFrom MaRDI portal\n\n\nDOI10.1007/BF00383399MaRDI QIDQ1182061zbMATH OpenFDO\n\nAuthors James D. Currie, Terry I. Visentin\n\nPublication date 27 June 1992\n\nPublished in Order (Search for Journal in Brave)\n\nFull work available at URL https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00383399\n\nzbMATH Keywords\n\nasymptoticposetsorder-preserving maplattices paths\n\nMathematics Subject Classification ID\n\nExact enumeration problems, generating functions (05A15) Asymptotic enumeration (05A16) Combinatorics of partially ordered sets (06A07)\n\nRecommendations\n\n  * The number of order-preserving maps between fences and crowns\n  * Enumeration of order preserving maps\n 